      contradictions: "AI investment↑ + data infrastructure↓: Companies announcing GenAI programmes while simultaneously operating on fragmented ERPs, partial DMS deployment, and non-existent master data governance. Without clean, integrated data, AI models produce worse outcomes than statistical forecasting. Board mandate vs. CSCO readiness gap: In three recent engagements, CSCO organisations had received GenAI mandates without board allocating budget for the data infrastructure prerequisite—a structural programme failure waiting to happen.",
      clientImplication: "CIOs and CSCOs receiving GenAI mandates need a sequenced approach: (1) data foundation assessment before AI investment, (2) use case selection based on data readiness not technology hype, (3) operating model design for AI-assisted SC decision-making.",
      thoucentriqAngle: "GenAI SC Readiness Assessment (3-4 weeks): data infrastructure gap analysis, use case prioritisation framework, technology stack selection, and change management readiness. Followed by AI-Enabled SC Transformation for selected use cases (demand sensing, procurement intelligence, distribution optimisation).",
      kpiLinkage: "SC Technology Maturity Score — India mid-tier: 2.4 avg vs. 4.8 P&G benchmark; Demand Forecast Accuracy — AI-enabled companies: 80%+ vs. statistical-only: 62-68%; Procurement Savings — AI-driven procurement: 3.5% vs. traditional: 0.7-1.5%",
      signalCluster: "India EPR Enforcement Escalates; HUL Q4 FY25 Revenue Growth 7% but Volume Under Pressure",
      trajectoryContext: "FY22-23 (Past): GenAI was a research topic for FMCG. P&G and Unilever were piloting. India FMCG companies had no AI in SC. → FY24-25 (Current): Board-level GenAI mandates everywhere. Pilots launched, mostly failing due to data readiness gaps. P&G scaled to 50+ use cases while India mid-tier is stuck in pilot-1. → Direction: Gap between global AI adopters and India mid-tier will expand unless data infrastructure prerequisite is addressed. → Inflection: FY26 is the 'use case vs. pilot graveyard' decision year—companies either scale 2-3 proven use cases or write off pilot investments.",
      financialImpact: "For a ₹10,000 Cr India FMCG: AI-enabled demand sensing improvement (10% DFA gain) = ₹150-250 Cr working capital release. AI procurement intelligence: 1-2% COGS savings = ₹400-800 Cr EBIT. Total AI-enabled SC value: ₹600-1,000 Cr over 3 years. Cost of failed pilots without data foundation: ₹50-200 Cr wasted.",
