      contradictions: "Premium positioning vs. infrastructure readiness: L'Oréal, Nestlé, and Mars are all pursuing premiumisation strategies in India while the cold chain infrastructure for premium delivery formats (chilled, frozen) covers only top-20 cities. Premium pricing requires premium distribution—the gap between aspiration and infrastructure is the largest in these categories. Private investment vs. government dependency: Most FMCG companies in interviews cite cold chain as a government infrastructure problem. But Amul's ₹350 Cr FY26 capex announcement and HCCB's cooler programme demonstrate the competitive advantage from proprietary investment.",
